    {
      "id": "x9ys38p",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Mechanism of Indian Monsoon"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Indian monsoon originates due to differential heating between the Indian landmass and surrounding oceans. In summer, the land heats rapidly creating a low-pressure area, while the Indian Ocean remains relatively cooler. This pressure difference draws moisture-laden winds toward India.",
      "id": "qzgjmaw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The monsoon mechanism is strengthened by the northward shift of the Inter-Tropical Convergence Zone (ITCZ), intense heating of the Tibetan Plateau, and changes in upper air circulation.",
      "id": "xh09xwj"
    },
    {
      "id": "v3vsh3i",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Component</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Role in Monsoon</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Importance</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>ITCZ</p>",
            "<p>Shifts north in summer pulling moist winds.</p>",
            "<p>Foundation concept</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Tibetan Plateau</p>",
            "<p>Intense heating creates strong low pressure.</p>",
            "<p>Frequently asked</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Subtropical Jet Stream</p>",
            "<p>Moves north allowing monsoon onset.</p>",
            "<p>Advanced concept</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mascarene High</p>",
            "<p>High pressure pushes winds toward India.</p>",
            "<p>Rare but scoring</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
